 collected on select Disney attractions or captured by one of the hundreds of Disney PhotoPass photographers. With Memory Maker, all those special moments will put smiles on your faces for years to come!\n\nHere's a tip for you: Be sure to ask your Disney PhotoPass photographers if they have any magic shots available. I don't want to ruin any surprises for you, but if they do, you'll see a bit of extra pixie dust within your pictures once they show up in your account!\n\nThanks so much for visiting us at the Disney Parks Moms Panel, Deena, and come back and see us again if you have any other questions! I hope that you and your entire group have a truly magical vacation!\n\nMeet the Panelist: Missy, Indiana\n\nHi! I'm Missy, a homeschool mom and part-time music teacher from Indiana. With a husband and five kids, I understand what busy family life is all about and how important it is to get away and create magical moments with your loved ones. I also believe planning is half the fun, so I'd be honored to help you plan your Walt Disney World Resort vacation!Learn More About Missy\n\nDidn't find what you were looking for?\n\nTo submit your question, please sign in now if you have not already done so.\n\nAsk the Disney Parks Moms Panel\n\nDiscover the magic of a Disney Parks family vacation from one of our knowledgeable online Panelists.\n\nThis is a question and answer forum to help you plan the best possible Disney vacation. Due to a high volume of submissions, we cannot guarantee that all questions will be answered. Also, please keep the number of questions in each submission to a limit of 3.\n\nWhen submitting a question, please do not provide us with ideas or suggestions. Your completion of this form constitutes your consent to our free and unrestricted use and disclosure of the information you provide to us.\n\nWrite Your Question\n\n256 Characters Remaining\n\nRelevant Tags\n\nAdd at least two tags relevant to your question from the choices below.\n\nThanks for su